.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-RUN\-GROUP\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-simulation-run-group-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-run\-group\-create \- Create a run group
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation run\-group create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Groups several simulation runs so they read as one, and starts generating the group report: one document across every run, with a scorecard summed across them and the issues found, each merged from the per\-run debriefs. Send `simulationRunPlanJobIds` to group runs that already exist (runs still in progress are fine: the report waits for them). Send `simulationRunPlanIds` to start one run of each plan and group those; this places real calls, exactly as starting each plan would. Poll GET /v1/simulation/run\-group/{groupId} until `latestReport.status` is READY.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/simulation/run\-group
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
What to call the group. Defaults to the plans' names when starting plans, and to the runs' plan names when grouping existing runs. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-simulation\-run\-plan\-job\-ids\fR \fI<value>\fR
Runs that already exist, in display order (2 to 20). Runs still in progress are fine: the group report waits for them. Send this or `simulationRunPlanIds`, not both. Repeatable. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-simulation\-run\-plan\-ids\fR \fI<value>\fR
Plans to run once each, in display order (2 to 20). Each plan starts a run, exactly as POST /v1/simulation/plan/{planId}/job would. Send this or `simulationRunPlanJobIds`, not both. Repeatable. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
